Here's a simple program that reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file:
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main()
{
    int wordCount = 0;
    string line;
    ifstream file("example.txt");
    while (getline(file, line)) {
        istringstream iss(line);
        while (iss >> wordCount) {
            if (iss.eos()) {
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    file.close();
    return 0;
}
```
This program opens a file called "example.txt" and reads it line by line. It uses an `istringstream` object to parse each line and count the number of occurrences of the word. If the end of the file is reached, the program breaks out of the inner loop. When the loop is finished, the program closes the file and returns 0 to indicate success.

